## Why TypeScript with React?

TypeScript adds **static typing** to JavaScript. Instead of discovering bugs at runtime (when users see them), TypeScript catches them at **compile time** (before you ship).

Benefits in React:
- Autocomplete for props in your IDE
- Immediate error when you pass the wrong prop type
- Self-documenting components (props are always explicit)
- Safer refactoring across large codebases

