## Chapter Summary

- TypeScript adds static types that catch bugs before runtime
- Type your props with an `interface` or `type`
- `useState` infers types automatically — add generics when initial value is `null`
- Type events with `React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>`, `React.FormEvent`, etc.
- Type `useRef` with the DOM element type: `useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null)`
- TypeScript makes your components self-documenting — no more guessing prop names

