## Chapter Summary

- Zustand creates global stores with a simple `create()` function
- Components subscribe to only the state slices they need — no unnecessary re-renders
- No Provider wrapping required anywhere
- Use `set()` to update state, `get()` to read state inside actions
- The `persist` middleware automatically saves state to localStorage
- Perfect for: cart, auth, theme, filters, UI state shared across pages

## React vs Next.js

React is a UI library — it handles components and state. Next.js is a **full-stack React framework** that adds:

| Feature | React (Vite) | Next.js |
|---------|-------------|---------|
| Routing | Manual (React Router) | Automatic (file-based) |
| Data fetching | useEffect / client-side | Server Components (no useEffect!) |
| SEO | Poor (JS renders late) | Excellent (HTML pre-rendered) |
| API endpoints | Separate backend required | Built-in API routes |
| Image optimization | Manual | Automatic |
| Performance | Good | Excellent (SSR + streaming) |

