## Server Components — Fetch Data Without useEffect

```jsx
// app/page.jsx — This is a SERVER Component by default!
// No "use client" directive = runs on the server

async function HomePage() {
  // Fetch directly in the component — no useEffect, no useState, no loading state
  const res = await fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts?_limit=5')
  const posts = await res.json()

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Latest Posts</h1>
      <ul>
        {posts.map(post => (
          <li key={post.id}>
            <a href={'/blog/' + post.id}>{post.title}</a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </main>
  )
}

export default HomePage
```

```text
How it works:
1. Next.js runs the component on the SERVER
2. The fetch happens server-side (fast, no CORS)
3. The HTML is pre-rendered with the data already in it
4. The browser receives ready-made HTML — no loading spinner!
```

